# Stereochemistry: tetrahedral centres and double-bond geometry.
#
# Every line here was a pinned gap until #191 — the parser rejected chirality
# markers and directional bonds outright, so none of them loaded at all. They
# now parse and round-trip.
#
# The reversed spellings are the ones worth keeping: `C(/F)=C/F` carries the
# same two `/` as `F/C=C/F` and means the opposite, because the first marker
# is written pointing away from the double bond. A writer and a parser that
# disagree about that sign flip cis and trans between them.

N[C@@H](C)C(=O)O l-alanine
N[C@H](C)C(=O)O d-alanine
F/C=C/F trans
F/C=C\F cis
C(/F)=C/F trans-reversed-spelling
C(\F)=C/F cis-reversed-spelling
O[C@H]1CC[C@@H](O)CC1 trans-cyclohexanediol
